In this paper, we introduce EdgeProfiler, a fast profiling framework designed to systematically evaluate the performance of lightweight LLMs in resource-constrained environments. The findings indicate that aggressive quantization significantly reduces the memory and computational requirements of lightweight LLMs, enabling practical deployment on resource-constrained edge devices. The slight impact on model accuracy is outweighed by improvements in memory efficiency and faster inference speeds. Reduced energy consumption from low-bit precision enhances feasibility for power-limited environments, such as mobile devices and microcontrollers. Careful quantization strategies and efficient hardware utilization bridge the gap between LLM capabilities and the limitations of edge systems, paving the way for broader and more practical applications.
The main contributions of this paper are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
    \item We introduce EdgeProfiler, a fast profiling framework for lightweight LLMs on edge devices.
    \item Systematic evaluation of quantization and low-bit implementations to address memory and power constraints.
    \item Analysis of strategies to enable LLM inference on microcontrollers and low-power edge platforms.
    \item Comprehensive review of recent research and experimental results on deploying LLMs in hardware-constrained environments.
\end{itemize}


