\subsection{Convergence of Proposed Algorithm}
Fig. \ref{converge_result} illustrates the convergence behavior of the proposed method under a fair comparison setting, where the locations of the AP and IIoT-(I) devices are set to $\mathbf{q}_\textrm{AP}=(0,0,5)$, $\mathbf{q}_\textrm{s}=(20,10,0)$, respectively, while the IIoT-(II) devices are uniform randomly distributed at a distance of $80$ m from the AP, and the RIS is deployed at $\mathbf{q}_\text{RIS}=(25,0,10)$. The AP is equipped with $N=8$ antennas along with an RIS comprising $M=32$ elements. Each case in the proposed \textit{SO \& ISAC} method is configured by varying the minimum rate threshold of the IIoT-(II) devices. As shown in Fig. \ref{converge_result}, all cases converge within $16$ iterations. It is observed that a lower minimum rate threshold leads to a higher proportion of the SO band usage, thereby achieving a lower estimation error. For instance, when $R_k^{th}=4$ Mbps, the optimized bandwidth splitting ratio is $\alpha=0.41$, while for $R_k^{th}=1$ Mbps, the optimal $\alpha$ is increased to $0.94$. With optimized variables, the performance gain is attributed to the increased bandwidth allocated for the IIoT-(I) sensing in the SO band, which effectively enhances the estimation accuracy.

% Fig. \ref{converge_result}은 제안된 알고리즘의 수렴성을 보여준다. 공정한 비교를 위해, 각 벤치마크는 모두 RIS의 x location = 25(m), user의 수는 3명, Ap의 안테나 수 N = 8개, 그리고 with a given number of RIS reflectors (M = 32)의 환경을 따른다. 각 벤치마크는 IIoT device의 만족해야하는 minimum rate을 기준으로 설정했다. Fig. \ref{converge_result}에서 보인것처럼, 모든 벤치마크는 iteration 16회 이내로 converge함을 보였다. 만족해야하는 minimum rate 값이 낮을 수록 communication을 위한 ISAC band의 할당 비율 대비 sensing을 위한 SO band의 할당 비율이 높아져 estimation error가 줄어듬을 확인할 수 있다.

