Radiological control, including radiation surveys and contamination measurements using smear tests, was performed on equipment leaving the material airlock, as well as on tools and PPE exiting the working area. After each intervention involving a risk of contamination, the area was cleaned using dedicated RP vacuum cleaners for classified areas. Smear tests and surface contamination measurements were then conducted. Prior to any roof opening, a waiting period was observed to allow for a complete air exchange in the working area.

