\subsection*{Observations}
To study general patterns in the data, we combined survey responses for each part (i.e., for the Zero Context answers and for the Minimal Context answers) in the following way. For every integer $i$ in the given ranges (see Table \ref{tab:intranges}), we find $k$ such that $i\text{ }\%\text{ }10 = k$. The fraction of responses for each $k$ are plotted in Figure \ref{fig:numMod10}. For example, the fraction of responses for $k = 1$ includes the options 1, 31, and 81. Following are some general observations from these results.

