denotes the minimum amount of capital required, conditionally at node $(X,i)$, to superhedge the value of the trajectory $X^2$  at terminal time $N(X)$, with $0\leq i\leq N(X)$, using the available  trajectories of the single asset $X^1$. %the payoff $F$.
