We mention a couple more implicit restrictions on our trajectory sets. Historically, all observed time intervals $\It=[t_0, t_0+T]$ for $t_0=-T, -2T-1, \hdots$  are of length $T$. Therefore, we restrict our trajectories to evolve for no longer than time $T$ into the future; essentially we are simulating one time interval's length of time into the future.\\

