\section{Methodology} \label{sec:Methodology}

This study employs a systematic, multi-stage methodology to evaluate the capability of a Large Language Model (LLM) to assess the economic soundness and theoretical consistency of applied spatial econometrics research. The process encompasses four core stages: targeted paper selection, standardized information extraction and summary creation, generation of counterfactual summaries, and a structured two-phase LLM evaluation protocol applied to both original and counterfactual summaries, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:workflow}.

% --- TikZ Schema ---
