Therefore, the response at relatively short times resembles the response of a Newtonian fluid, indicating that the parameter $\beta$ modulates the initial lubrication force. In the case of an upper-convected Maxwell fluid, i.e., for $\beta = 0$, the force will start from zero, and, for $\beta = 1$, the force will align with the expected reaction of a Newtonian fluid.
