\subsection{Comparison between methods}

One of the main contributions of the \package{} is that its single coherent framework allows for
easy comparisons of different algorithms from the literature. 
As a simple example, in \Cref{fig:signal_comparison}, we compare the different estimates of the
smooth signal from \Cref{fig:signals} for the \pythoninline{Landweber}, \pythoninline{TruncatedSVD}
and \pythoninline{ConjugateGradients}-classes, respectively. 
While there is no clear structural difference between the \pythoninline{Landweber} and
\pythoninline{ConjugateGradients} estimate, the spectral cutoff of \pythoninline{TruncatedSVD} is markedly visible.

