provides a clear explanation for why the stopping times mostly stay below 50.
Both in the weak and the strong risk, this is enough to loose adaptivity.
However, this can be salvaged by applying the two-step procedure from \eqref{eq:two_step_tSVD}, since
we only lose about a factor of five in the computational load from the deviations in the stopping time.

