services provided by the JTPA. The outcome of interest $Y$ is the total individual earnings in the 30 months after program
assignment.\footnote{We take the intention-to-treat perspective. One may also consider an net-of-cost outcome, which would further deduct 774 dollars for each of  those assigned to treatment.} The study also collected a variety of the applicants' background information ($X$), some of which might be perceived  as sensitive, e.g.,  gender, race and marital
